   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 435 of the laws of 2014 amending the environmental\nconservation law relating to defining spearguns and allowing recreational\nspearfishing in New York's marine and coastal waters, in relation to extending\nthe effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S10531",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S10531-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Chap 435 of 2014",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S10531\n\nSPONSOR: SKOUFIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 435 of the laws of 2014 amending the environ-\nmental conservation law relating to defining spearguns and allowing\nrecreational spearfishing in New York's marine and coastal waters, in\nrelation to extending the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to extend the provisions allowing for recre-\national spearfishing in New York's marine and coastal waters, for three\nyears.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Extends for three years the provisions of Section 3 of Chap-\nter 435 of the Laws of 2014 amending the Environmental Conservation Law\nrelating to defining spearguns and allowing recreational spearfishing in\nNew York's marine and coastal waters.\n\nSection 2: Sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe law which allowed for recreational spearfishing in New York's marine\nand coastal waters sunsets on June 1, 2026. This legislation is neces-\nsary to extend the effectiveness of that law to June 1, 2029.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nSenate\n\n2023: S2724A, Chapter 149 of 2023.\n\nAssembly\n\n2023: A6107, Chapter 149 of 2023.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
